Key structures:
- `enumerate_preorders(n)`: iterate over all relations as bitmask of n*n pairs; reflexive + transitive. n=4 → 65536 iterations, fine.
- Chains: all sequences of distinct indices where for consecutive elements rel[a][b] (with a before b in the sequence). To keep the "distinct order", require rel[seq[i]][seq[j]] for i<j; sequences of distinct indices suffice (reflexivity not an issue). For n=4, all permutations of all subsets: 65 sequences (including length 1).
- I+ subsets: nonempty subsets of {0..n-1} (as q points). 15 for n=4.
- J[q] = frozenset(i for i in range(n) if rel[i][q]).
- S(seq, J, Ip) = any(seq[t0:] ⊆ J[q] ...). 
- U_full(seq,J,Ip) = all points in union.
- U_tail(seq,J,Ip) = any(seq[t0:] ⊆ union).
- Checks C1: S⟹U_full; C2: U_full⟹S; C3: U_tail⟺U_full and U_tail⟹S.

